      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We present the case of an 86-year-old female with stenosis of the anomalous left main trunk originating from a stenosed ostial right coronary artery. She underwent successful percutaneous coronary intervention using simultaneous sirolimus-eluting kissing stents (SKS) for anomalous bifurcating lesions."},
